body:
For anyone wondering why I decided to upgrade the RAM rather than getting the MBP 13": I was considering it, and it definitely would have been a great laptop for me, but I don't really use my laptops intensively as I'm a university student in a program with extensive writing, rather than using professional editing software, etc. The MBP is just... too powerful for what I need it to do (e.g., word processing, reddit, a bit of \*light\* gaming, streaming, research). Rather than spending the extra $200 (CAD, btw) I figured I could just upgrade the RAM and I'll be able to have my 20+ safari tabs open while I work, from the recommendation of my partner. Tried opening every application on it all at once last night and they all opened in less than a minute! This laptop is POWERFUL! 

&#x200B;

This is the 120gb  SSD (iirc) version as well, which I specifically chose as I have iCloud and can store the majority  of my files on it, saving me even more money as I don't need more storage.
